title: "Erdős Problem #203: no pure finite prime covering with period dividing lcm(1,...,17) = 12,252,240"
abstract: "A partial result on Erdős Problem #203: no pure finite prime covering has period dividing N = lcm(1,...,17) = 12,252,240. The complete prime pool of gcd(2^N-1, 3^N-1) has 192 primes. Using the slope-one line method and 5/7 cut of Erdős Problem a Day (P. White and Claude, 14 October 2026), explicit non-uniform weights modulo 60 give the exact bound 3961943/4084080 < 1. Of the 480 divisors of N, 411 had already been excluded by that earlier work; the 69 new periods are listed with a script that reproduces the list. Includes the research draft, the certificate data, three verifiers and the verification record. The full problem remains open; not peer reviewed."
